meta {
  name: Sync Steam Playtimes (Stream)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{backendUrl}}/api/user/steam/sync/stream
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

docs {
  SSE variant of "Sync Steam Playtimes" (media_type: text/event-stream):
  emits a `progress` event ({"processed", "total"}) after every game
  considered, then a final `done` event carrying the same entry list
  "Sync Steam Playtimes" returns directly, or an `error` event in its
  place if the sync fails partway through.

  Bruno's plain HTTP request type has no special SSE handling, so
  running this here just returns the raw concatenated event-stream body
  once the connection closes rather than showing live progress - use a
  real SSE/EventSource client to see incremental updates. Run
  auth/Login and user/Set Steam ID first.

  503 if neither the caller nor the server has a Steam Web API key
  configured - this is a real top-level HTTP response, raised before
  the SSE stream opens. A missing Steam ID, by contrast, surfaces as an
  `error` event inside an HTTP 200 stream, not as a 400.
}
